    },
    {
      "claim": "Every admitted marker creates a separate guidance publication before pruning. The held projection is advanced only at segment seal, so k controls induce k(k-1)/2+k replayed suffix applications, excluding planner and shell event applications.",
      "kind": "source-derived"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Control round7 settlement has234 controls. Actual retained-event core suffix replay performed27495 applications in124.120458443 seconds. One pass over those same234 controls took1.009902299 seconds. Every recorded pre-state and final complete state matched.",
      "kind": "observed"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The same experiment at control round1 used88 controls,3916 suffix applications and0.891245762 seconds, versus0.022081939 seconds for a single pass.",
      "kind": "observed"
    },
    {
      "claim": "All retained journal envelopes and digest chains decoded successfully; pure decoding took0.004985279/0.005158274/0.007235308 seconds for control/planted/deep-probe. This does not measure synchronized journal publication.",
      "kind": "observed"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The selected58423832-byte retained three-VM snapshot loaded/validated in9.376321364 seconds; repeated store puts took2.849754367 and2.910977332 seconds and preserved exact BLAKE3 byte identity. No control or planted finding required this store path.",
      "kind": "observed"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Repeated staged suffix validation is a major contributor to the campaign timing gap: the exact subpath independently reproduces minute-scale work without KVM or disk synchronization. It is not an exact attribution of the original whole-round timing.",
      "kind": "inference"
    }
